 "text": {
  "what": "The Mentawai islands, west of Sumatra: long lines laid along arms, chest and legs, added to at each stage of a life.",
  "story": "*Inference —* the Mentawai case is the clearest example of a pattern this site keeps meeting: a tradition is called dying for a century and is still there, thinner, with the elders carrying it and the state having spent decades discouraging it."
 },
